---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import PartnerBadges from '../components/PartnerBadges.astro';
import ClientLogos from '../components/ClientLogos.astro';
import ServiceLinks from '../components/ServiceLinks.astro';

const faqs = [
  { q: "What is POAS and how is it different from ROAS?", a: "ROAS measures revenue against ad spend. POAS measures profit against ad spend after product cost, fulfilment and fees. A campaign can deliver strong ROAS while still being unprofitable if margins are thin. Setting a POAS target before campaigns launch lets every pound of ad spend be judged against a profit outcome." },
  { q: "Which Meta platforms do you advertise on?", a: "Meta ads can run across Facebook, Instagram and Messenger. The best placements differ by account, so judge them on where your audience spends time and where creative performs for your product category." },
  { q: "Do you create Meta ad creative?", a: "Creative is not included in the Visible Ads management fee. Good Meta creative usually means static images, carousels and video concepts tailored to each audience segment and funnel stage, with structured testing to find winning concepts and retire underperformers. Ask any agency what is included and what is quoted separately." },
  { q: "Should I use Advantage+ sales campaigns or manual campaigns?", a: "The choice depends on your tracking, product range and creative supply. Advantage+ sales campaigns suit ecommerce accounts with reliable purchase tracking, a catalogue and a steady flow of creative. Meta's system makes more of the delivery decisions there. Manual campaigns suit cases where you need control over audiences, placements or budget by segment. They also suit low purchase volume. Whichever structure you choose, judge it against your POAS target and treat the platform's own ROAS as a weekly signal only." },
  { q: "How many ads do I need to test on Meta?", a: "Enough distinct concepts for the system to find a winner and no more than your budget can read. A sensible plan is a small set of genuinely different ideas in a few formats, tested against each other, with the weakest retired and replaced on a schedule you agree. A smaller budget means fewer tests at a time." },
  { q: "Why do my Meta numbers not match my shop or GA4?", a: "Meta credits sales using its own attribution settings and a total can include modelled (estimated) conversions. Your shop records actual orders, and GA4 applies its own attribution. The numbers rarely match. A stable gap can be normal. Reconcile Meta, GA4 and order data on one defined basis before changing spend. The guide to the Meta Ads and GA4 revenue mismatch shows how." },
  { q: "What does Meta Business Partner mean?", a: "Meta Business Partner is a Meta programme for agencies and other providers. Visible Ads holds that status. It is Meta's recognition of the agency and carries no guarantee of results for your account." },
  { q: "How much does Meta ads management cost?", a: "Fees are per channel plus VAT. Silver is £1,000 a month for ad budgets up to £3,000. Gold is £1,500 a month for budgets up to £20,000. Platinum is £2,000 a month plus 5% for budgets above £20,000. Creative is not included. Meta and Google need a one-off £1,000 tracking setup. The minimum term is three months and then it rolls monthly on 30 days notice." },
  { q: "What budget do I need for Meta ads?", a: "Visible Ads does not publish a minimum ad spend. Silver covers ad budgets up to £3,000 a month. A larger budget allows more creative and audience testing at once, and a smaller one means fewer tests. Set spend relative to your break-even ROAS and POAS target, because profit is not guaranteed at any budget." },
  { q: "What happens after I ask for a Meta ads audit?", a: "You get an initial response within one working day. The audit looks at your unit economics, tracking and current Meta structure and sets out where scaling could be tested against profit." },
];

const schema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@graph": [
    {
      "@type": "Service",
      "name": "Meta Ads Agency, Facebook & Instagram Advertising",
      "provider": {
        "@type": "Organization",
        "name": "Visible Ads",
        "url": "https://visible-ads.com"
      },
      "description": "Meta Business Partner. Facebook and Instagram campaign management for ecommerce brands, judged on Profit on Ad Spend (POAS) and unit economics, not just ROAS.",
      "url": "https://visible-ads.com/paid-social/",
      "serviceType": "Meta Ads & Paid Social Media Advertising",
      "areaServed": "GB"
    },
    {
      "@type": "FAQPage",
      "mainEntity": faqs.map((f) => ({
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": f.q,
        "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": f.a }
      }))
    },
    {
      "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
      "itemListElement": [
        { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 1, "name": "Home", "item": "https://visible-ads.com/" },
        { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 2, "name": "Meta Ads", "item": "https://visible-ads.com/paid-social/" }
      ]
    }
  ]
};
---

<Layout title="Meta Ads Agency | Facebook & Instagram | Visible Ads" description="Meta Business Partner. Facebook and Instagram campaigns judged on Profit on Ad Spend (POAS) and unit economics, not just ROAS. Get a free Meta ads audit." schema={schema}>

  <!-- Hero -->
  <section class="relative py-20 lg:py-28 overflow-hidden bg-navy" data-animate>
    <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-gradient-to-br from-navy via-pink-900 to-navy-light"></div>
    <div class="absolute inset-0 dot-pattern opacity-10"></div>
    <div class="relative max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <div class="max-w-3xl">
        <span class="inline-block px-4 py-1.5 bg-electric/20 text-electric-light text-sm font-medium rounded-full mb-6">Meta Business Partner</span>
        <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl lg:text-5xl font-heading font-extrabold text-white leading-tight mb-6">Meta Ads That Scale on Unit Profit, Not Vanity Metrics</h1>
        <p class="text-lg sm:text-xl text-slate-light mb-8 leading-relaxed">Visible Ads manages Facebook and Instagram ad campaigns for ecommerce brands, with Profit on Ad Spend (POAS) and unit economics as the yardstick. UK social media advertising grew 21% to £11.5bn in 2025 (IAB UK Digital Adspend 2025, published 3 March 2026), which is overall UK social spend, not ecommerce alone.</p>
        <p class="text-white font-semibold mb-3">What good Meta management covers</p>
        <ul class="text-slate-light mb-8 space-y-2 list-disc pl-5">
          <li>A break-even ROAS and target POAS worked out before launch</li>
          <li>Advantage+ or manual campaign structure chosen to fit your account</li>
          <li>Conversions API tracking checked against your orders (Meta and Google tracking setup is a one-off £1,000)</li>
          <li>Creative concepts and a structured testing plan (creative is not included in the fee)</li>
          <li>Weekly budget rules and reporting against profit</li>
        </ul>
        <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-4">
          <a href="/free-ads-audit" class="w-full sm:w-auto inline-flex items-center justify-center bg-cta text-white font-semibold px-8 py-4 rounded-xl hover:bg-electric transition-colors text-lg">Get Your Free Meta Ads Audit</a>
          <a href="/contact/" class="w-full sm:w-auto inline-flex items-center justify-center text-white font-medium px-8 py-4 rounded-xl border border-white/20 hover:bg-white/10 transition-colors">Talk to Us About Meta Ads</a>
        </div>
        <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-slate-light">Initial response within one working day. <a href="#poas" class="underline hover:text-white">Why POAS matters</a></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Partner Badges -->
  <section class="py-12 bg-sky-tint border-y border-gray-100">
    <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <PartnerBadges compact />
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Buyer guidance -->
  <section class="py-20 lg:py-28 bg-white" data-animate>
    <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-12 items-center">
          <div>
            <span class="inline-block px-3 py-1 bg-electric/10 text-electric text-sm font-semibold rounded-full mb-4">Buyer guidance</span>
            <h2 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-heading font-bold text-navy mb-6">What to Ask Any Meta Ads Agency</h2>
            <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-6">Meta advertising decides much of its own delivery, so the agency's judgement shows up in tracking, creative and budget rules. Ask who will run your account, which results they track and how often they report.</p>
            <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">Visible Ads is a founder-led, London-based Meta Business Partner. For how Meta fits alongside search, shopping and marketplaces, see the <a href="/ecommerce-ppc-agency/" class="text-electric underline hover:text-electric-dark">ecommerce PPC agency</a> page.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="bg-sky-tint rounded-2xl p-8 border border-gray-100">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-heading font-bold text-navy mb-4">Questions worth asking</h3>
            <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
              <li>How is break-even ROAS worked out for my margins?</li>
              <li>How are purchase events checked against my real orders?</li>
              <li>What creative is included and what is quoted separately?</li>
              <li>What rules decide when budget goes up or down?</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- POAS Section -->
  <section id="poas" class="py-20 lg:py-28 bg-sky-tint" data-animate>
    <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
        <div class="text-center mb-12">
          <h2 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-heading font-bold text-navy mb-4">Judge Meta Ads on POAS, Profit on Ad Spend</h2>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 max-w-2xl mx-auto">ROAS tells you revenue. POAS tells you whether you are making money. Profit is the goal and ROAS is the lever managed week to week.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-8 mb-12">
          <div class="bg-white rounded-2xl p-8 border border-gray-100 shadow-sm">
            <div class="w-12 h-12 bg-gray-100 rounded-xl flex items-center justify-center mb-4">
              <span class="text-sm font-bold text-gray-400">ROAS</span>
            </div>
            <h3 class="text-xl font-heading font-bold text-navy mb-3">Return on Ad Spend</h3>
            <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4">Revenue generated per pound spent on ads. A useful weekly signal that is incomplete on its own.</p>
            <p class="text-gray-600 text-sm leading-relaxed">A 5x ROAS on a 15% margin product means you are losing money on every sale. ROAS ignores product cost, fulfilment, fees and returns. It cannot tell you whether a campaign is actually profitable.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="bg-navy rounded-2xl p-8 border border-electric/20 shadow-sm relative overflow-hidden">
            <div class="absolute top-0 right-0 w-24 h-24 bg-electric/10 rounded-full -translate-y-8 translate-x-8"></div>
            <div class="relative z-10">
              <div class="w-12 h-12 bg-electric/20 rounded-xl flex items-center justify-center mb-4">
                <span class="text-sm font-bold text-electric">POAS</span>
              </div>
              <h3 class="text-xl font-heading font-bold text-white mb-3">Profit on Ad Spend</h3>
              <p class="text-slate-light leading-relaxed mb-4">Gross profit generated per pound spent on ads after product cost, fees and fulfilment.</p>
              <p class="text-slate-light/80 text-sm leading-relaxed">POAS is the target. ROAS is the lever used week to week to hit it. Setting a POAS target before campaigns launch grounds scaling decisions in what the business can afford to spend.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-white rounded-2xl p-8 border border-electric/20">
          <h3 class="text-xl font-heading font-bold text-navy mb-4">Unit Economics First</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">Map your unit economics before building a campaign. That covers product cost, fees, fulfilment and return rate, and it gives you a break-even ROAS and a target POAS. Budget decisions and creative tests can then be measured against that number, and spend that pushes you below your profit threshold is the signal to stop scaling.</p>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mt-6 leading-relaxed">Read <a href="/blog/meta-ads-vs-google-ads-ecommerce/" class="text-electric underline hover:text-electric-dark">Meta Ads vs Google Ads for ecommerce</a> for help comparing channels for your ecommerce business. Use the <a href="/meta-ads-ga4-revenue-mismatch" class="text-electric underline hover:text-electric-dark">Meta Ads and GA4 reconciliation guide</a> before changing spend if Meta revenue and GA4 disagree.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Services -->
  <section class="py-20 lg:py-28 bg-white" data-animate>
    <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <div class="text-center mb-16">
        <h2 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-heading font-bold text-navy mb-4">Meta Ads Services</h2>
        <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 max-w-2xl mx-auto">Full-funnel Facebook and Instagram advertising, from brand awareness to purchase to repeat customer.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-6 max-w-5xl mx-auto">
        <div class="bg-sky-tint rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
          <div class="w-10 h-10 bg-electric/10 rounded-lg flex items-center justify-center mb-4">
            <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-electric" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M15 10l4.553-2.069A1 1 0 0121 8.82v6.36a1 1 0 01-1.447.894L15 14M5 18h8a2 2 0 002-2V8a2 2 0 00-2-2H5a2 2 0 00-2 2v8a2 2 0 002 2z"/></svg>
          </div>
          <h3 class="font-heading font-bold text-navy mb-2">Facebook & Instagram Ads</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm">Prospecting and conversion campaigns across Feed, Stories and Reels. Audience structures work best when built around your ideal customer profile and POAS targets.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-sky-tint rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
          <div class="w-10 h-10 bg-electric/10 rounded-lg flex items-center justify-center mb-4">
            <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-electric" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M4 16l4.586-4.586a2 2 0 012.828 0L16 16m-2-2l1.586-1.586a2 2 0 012.828 0L20 14m-6-6h.01M6 20h12a2 2 0 002-2V6a2 2 0 00-2-2H6a2 2 0 00-2 2v12a2 2 0 002 2z"/></svg>
          </div>
          <h3 class="font-heading font-bold text-navy mb-2">Creative Strategy & Testing</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm">Creative is a major performance lever on Meta. Static, carousel and video concepts can be tested in a structured way to find winners and retire underperformers before they drain budget.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-sky-tint rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
          <div class="w-10 h-10 bg-electric/10 rounded-lg flex items-center justify-center mb-4">
            <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-electric" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M17 20h5v-2a3 3 0 00-5.356-1.857M17 20H7m10 0v-2c0-.656-.126-1.283-.356-1.857M7 20H2v-2a3 3 0 015.356-1.857M7 20v-2c0-.656.126-1.283.356-1.857m0 0a5.002 5.002 0 019.288 0M15 7a3 3 0 11-6 0 3 3 0 016 0z"/></svg>
          </div>
          <h3 class="font-heading font-bold text-navy mb-2">Audience Architecture</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm">Interest, lookalike and Advantage+ audience builds mapped to funnel stage. Start from who your best customers are, then build audiences that aim to find more of them at your POAS target.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-sky-tint rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
          <div class="w-10 h-10 bg-electric/10 rounded-lg flex items-center justify-center mb-4">
            <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-electric" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M4 4v5h.582m15.356 2A8.001 8.001 0 004.582 9m0 0H9m11 11v-5h-.581m0 0a8.003 8.003 0 01-15.357-2m15.357 2H15"/></svg>
          </div>
          <h3 class="font-heading font-bold text-navy mb-2">Retargeting Sequences</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm">Warm audiences, add-to-cart, view-content and past purchasers can get tailored ads matched to their stage in the buying journey. Retargeting often looks efficient on platform reporting, so check how much of it is incremental.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-sky-tint rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
          <div class="w-10 h-10 bg-electric/10 rounded-lg flex items-center justify-center mb-4">
            <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-electric" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M9 3v2m6-2v2M9 19v2m6-2v2M5 9H3m2 6H3m18-6h-2m2 6h-2M7 19h10a2 2 0 002-2V7a2 2 0 00-2-2H7a2 2 0 00-2 2v10a2 2 0 002 2zM9 9h6v6H9V9z"/></svg>
          </div>
          <h3 class="font-heading font-bold text-navy mb-2">Conversions API (CAPI)</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm">Server-side event tracking through the Conversions API sends purchase events from your server as well as the browser. Checking those events against your orders gives optimisation a firmer base, though no tracking setup is perfect.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-sky-tint rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
          <div class="w-10 h-10 bg-electric/10 rounded-lg flex items-center justify-center mb-4">
            <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-electric" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M9 19v-6a2 2 0 00-2-2H5a2 2 0 00-2 2v6a2 2 0 002 2h2a2 2 0 002-2zm0 0V9a2 2 0 012-2h2a2 2 0 012 2v10m-6 0a2 2 0 002 2h2a2 2 0 002-2m0 0V5a2 2 0 012-2h2a2 2 0 012 2v14a2 2 0 01-2 2h-2a2 2 0 01-2-2z"/></svg>
          </div>
          <h3 class="font-heading font-bold text-navy mb-2">Performance Reporting</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm">Reporting works best against POAS targets as well as ROAS, showing what campaigns cost per unit of profit and what is being changed to improve it.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Advantage+ vs manual -->
  <section id="advantage-plus" class="py-20 lg:py-28 bg-sky-tint" data-animate>
    <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
        <h2 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-heading font-bold text-navy mb-4">Advantage+ or Manual Campaigns: When Each Fits</h2>
        <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4">Advantage+ sales campaigns hand more delivery decisions to Meta's system. Manual campaigns keep them with you. Neither structure wins by default. The right one depends on your account.</p>
        <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4">Advantage+ sales campaigns automate more of the optimisation across creative, targeting, placements and budget. Manual campaigns offer more direct control over each of those settings.</p>
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-8 mt-8">
          <div class="bg-white rounded-2xl p-8 border border-gray-100 shadow-sm">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-heading font-bold text-navy mb-3">Advantage+ sales campaigns fit when</h3>
            <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 text-gray-700">
              <li>Purchase tracking is reliable and the order value is passed back correctly.</li>
              <li>You have a catalogue with enough products to give the system choice.</li>
              <li>You can keep a steady flow of different creative coming.</li>
              <li>The goal is purchases and you want less audience micromanagement.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div class="bg-white rounded-2xl p-8 border border-gray-100 shadow-sm">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-heading font-bold text-navy mb-3">Manual campaigns fit when</h3>
            <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 text-gray-700">
              <li>You need to control audiences, placements or budget by segment.</li>
              <li>Purchase volume is low and gives an automated system little to learn from.</li>
              <li>You are testing one variable, such as a single offer or audience.</li>
              <li>The goal is leads or another action that needs a specific conversion location.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
        <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mt-8">Start from your tracking, product range and creative supply. Pick the structure, judge it against your target POAS and change it if it is not earning its place.</p>
        <p class="mt-6"><a href="/free-ads-audit/" class="text-electric font-semibold underline hover:text-electric-dark">Get a free Meta ads audit of your current structure</a></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Creative volume and testing -->
  <section id="creative-testing" class="py-20 lg:py-28 bg-white" data-animate>
    <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
        <h2 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-heading font-bold text-navy mb-4">How Much Creative Meta Ads Need</h2>
        <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-6">Meta's system decides who sees which ad. Creative is the part you still control. It carries much of the result in any campaign. Advantage+ campaigns lean on it most because audience choices are largely automated.</p>
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-6">
          <div class="bg-sky-tint rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
            <h3 class="font-heading font-bold text-navy mb-2">Different ideas in every test</h3>
            <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm">A new headline on the same image is a variant. A new angle, offer or proof point is a concept. A sensible plan is a small set of genuinely different concepts in static, carousel and video formats.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="bg-sky-tint rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
            <h3 class="font-heading font-bold text-navy mb-2">Tests sized to your budget</h3>
            <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm">Each test needs enough purchases to read. A smaller budget means fewer concepts tested at once, so size the schedule to what your budget can support.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="bg-sky-tint rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
            <h3 class="font-heading font-bold text-navy mb-2">Judged on profit</h3>
            <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm">Winners and losers are called against your POAS target. A concept that gets cheap clicks but low-margin orders is a candidate for retirement. A refresh schedule helps stop ad fatigue creeping in.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mt-8">Creative production is quoted separately from the management fee. Decide early whether you will supply assets, commission them or use your own team.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Measurement -->
  <section id="measurement" class="py-20 lg:py-28 bg-sky-tint" data-animate>
    <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
        <h2 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-heading font-bold text-navy mb-4">Honest Meta Ads Measurement After iOS 14</h2>
        <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4">Reliable Meta reporting starts with reliable events. A common approach is to set up the Conversions API so purchase events and order values reach Meta from your server as well as the browser, then check them against your real orders.</p>
        <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4">Meta's Conversions API is designed to create a connection between your marketing data and Meta's systems. Meta says it helps <a href="https://developers.facebook.com/docs/marketing-api/conversions-api/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-electric underline hover:text-electric-dark">optimise ad targeting, decrease cost per result and measure outcomes</a>. It can run alongside the Meta Pixel, and server events are processed like pixel events.</p>
        <div class="bg-white rounded-2xl p-8 border border-gray-100 shadow-sm mb-6">
          <h3 class="text-xl font-heading font-bold text-navy mb-4">What a platform-reported number can and cannot tell you</h3>
          <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
            <div>
              <p class="font-semibold text-navy mb-2">It can show</p>
              <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 text-gray-700 text-sm">
                <li>Which ads, audiences and creative the platform credits with sales under your attribution settings.</li>
                <li>Direction of travel: whether results are improving week on week.</li>
                <li>Relative performance between concepts in the same account.</li>
              </ul>
            </div>
            <div>
              <p class="font-semibold text-navy mb-2">It cannot show</p>
              <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 text-gray-700 text-sm">
                <li>Your profit. The platform does not know product cost, fees, fulfilment or returns.</li>
                <li>Which sales would have happened anyway without the ad.</li>
                <li>How Meta, Google, Amazon and email overlap. Each platform reports from its own view.</li>
                <li>Which conversions are modelled estimates and which were observed directly once the two sit in one total.</li>
              </ul>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4">Treat Meta's figures as one view. Compare them with order data and GA4 on one defined basis and then set budget against profit. The guide on <a href="/meta-ads-ga4-revenue-mismatch/" class="text-electric underline hover:text-electric-dark">why Meta Ads ROAS and GA4 revenue do not match</a> gives a worked method. Meta and Google tracking setup is a one-off £1,000.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

